WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.270
Let’s look at the hips, and how they help you move every day.

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:12.040
A hip joint can be affected by PsA, causing pain, and making it harder to move.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:18.460
You may notice that steps, walking, or getting up from a chair are harder.

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.630
These examples help you describe a problem.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:26.170
They do not prove that PsA is the cause.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:31.420
Tell your team which side hurts, and what has changed.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:35.970
Mention a new limp, or trouble with a task you could do before.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.860
Keeping a healthy weight lowers the strain on your joints.

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:43.830
And it may help your medicines work better.

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:48.380
The team can check the hip, and the areas nearby.

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:51.870
Do not use the map to decide the cause on your own.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.940
Great job! Let’s review.

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:59.530
Pain or stiffness may limit movement.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:03.600
Tell your team which side hurts and what has changed.
